data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0385c9a4aab47c4b006a67772ff23c8192bc22c8d8df3ba9a9","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":393,"text":"We want the least common multiple (LCM) of 1,2,...,15. For each prime p ≤ 15, take the highest power p^k that is ≤ 15:\n\n- 2^3 = 8 (2^4 = 16 > 15)\n- 3^2 = 9 (3^3 = 27 > 15)\n- 5^1 = 5\n- 7^1 = 7\n- 11^1 = 11\n- 13^1 = 13\n\nThe LCM is the product of these highest prime powers:\nLCM = 2^3 · 3^2 · 5 · 7 · 11 · 13\n= 8 · 9 · 5 · 7 · 11 · 13\n= 360,360.\n\nThus the smallest positive integer divisible by every integer from 1 through 15 is 360,360."}

